---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { practice } from '../data/practice';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement | Abilene Eye Institute"
  description="Accessibility commitment and features of the Abilene Eye Institute website."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold text-navy-900">Accessibility statement</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        An eye care practice's website should work for people with low vision and for everyone who
        uses assistive technology. This site is built to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
        (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA, and to 2.2 AA where practical: strong color contrast, large readable
        text, visible keyboard focus, a skip-navigation link, semantic headings, descriptive labels,
        and support for reduced-motion settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        The self-assessment and all navigation work with a keyboard alone and with screen readers.
        No information is conveyed by color alone, and no text is baked into images. Every page is
        checked with automated accessibility testing at desktop and phone sizes; automated tools
        catch only part of what matters, so people review it too.
      </p>
      <p>
        If anything on this site is hard to use, please call
        <a href={practice.links.call} class="font-semibold text-navy-700 underline">{practice.phone.display}</a>
        and the office will help you directly and make sure it gets fixed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
